      "question": {
        ":question/id": "71b98d17-a449-5844-80cf-b608ab77000a",
        ":question/problem": "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 3 x^{2} e^{2 x^{3} + 3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}} $+C$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=2 x^{3} + 3$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(6 x^{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 3 x^{2} e^{2 x^{3} + 3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=e^{u}+C.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(e^{u}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\left(e^{2 x^{3} + 3}\\right)+C.\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "f07a55de-cbab-55d4-89f8-58bcff9cb751",
            ":answer-field/key": "answer",
            ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
            ":answer-field/choices": [
              {
                ":answer/id": "1b4967da-34df-5326-adef-a4a2e38a1818",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "\\frac{1}{2}\\left(e^{2 x^{3} + 3}\\right)"
              }
            ],
            ":answer-field/correct": [
              ":answer/id",
              "1b4967da-34df-5326-adef-a4a2e38a1818"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
