      "question": {
        ":question/id": "b5a9808d-04fd-57d0-8c1f-56acc1d05a06",
        ":question/problem": "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 4 x e^{2 x^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}} $+C$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=2 x^{2}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(4 x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 4 x e^{2 x^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=e^{u}+C.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\int e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=e^{u}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\ne^{2 x^{2}}+C.\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "9ac1486d-5749-5938-9322-c13e1a18c668",
